From: mscharged-port
Subject: Tweak: a live replay that catches up takes many steps a tick
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A replay takes more than one step in a fixed update's tick when it plays
faster (GetNetworkInputPlaybackExtraUpdates, tweak patch 0071), and a match
watched live from far behind its stream catches up as fast as the computer
can: its tick takes steps until they have used their share of the time.
After each step the port says whether the tick's steps end
(mscharged_tweak_replay_tick_over): the share is used, or the step began a
load (a cutscene's animations, a picture from the disc) that the next steps
must wait for, as they do at a tick's start. The steps left stay in the
replay for the next ticks; a match, and a replay at its own pace, takes one
step a tick as before.

Catching up, the steps would start sounds many times faster than the sounds
end, until the audio has no voice (AudioSampleSource::Initialize then
prepares a null one), no sliders (AllocateLocalAudioSliders) or no memory
for a streamed one (a crowd's reaction) left. While it catches up
(mscharged_tweak_replay_turbo) PlaySound and PlayOwnedSound start none but
the tracked sounds (the music, the captains' streams), as for a cue the
audio does not have. A replayed rollback step starts no sound either
(MSCHARGED_AUDIO_ACTION): sound is no part of the match's steps.

The match stands still while a cutscene plays, on each machine as long as
it lasts there; catching up, the replay skips every part a player may skip,
and the presentation's wipes before and after a cutscene run faster
(Wiper::Run, mscharged_tweak_replay_wipe_speed), as it waits for them.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_replay.h b/include/mscharged_replay.h
--- a/include/mscharged_replay.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_replay.h
@@ -44,6 +44,17 @@ bool mscharged_tweak_replay_read_input(int player, void* record, unsigned char*
 // Each fixed step while a replay plays: the steps its speed adds to the one
 // the router runs (-1 while it is paused: the step then runs none).
 int mscharged_tweak_replay_extra_updates(void);
+// After each step of a fixed update's tick (tweak patch 0086): whether the
+// tick's steps end there while a replay plays (a live one catching up used
+// the tick's share of the time, or the step began a load the next steps wait
+// for). False for a match.
+bool mscharged_tweak_replay_tick_over(void);
+// Whether a live replay catches up as fast as the computer can now: it
+// starts no sound but the tracked ones meanwhile, its sound being off.
+bool mscharged_tweak_replay_turbo(void);
+// How many times faster the wipes around cutscenes run: more than 1 while a
+// live replay catches up.
+float mscharged_tweak_replay_wipe_speed(void);
 // The title (passed as by Skip intro): whether it starts the replay's match
 // instead of going to the main menu, once; then, from its update, the start.
 bool mscharged_tweak_take_replay_start(void);
